    "q-71483": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71483",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y={log}_{2}⁡(2x+3).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={log}_{2}⁡(u),\\,u=2x+3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(2x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(2x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-71483-a",
